<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Breton Succession</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1341–<a href="/years/1364">1364</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Breton Succession was fought from 1341 to 1364 for the Duchy of Brittany between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-of-blois">Charles of Blois</a>, backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-montfort">John of Montfort</a> and his son, backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. Part of the wider <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>, it included the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/combat-of-the-thirty">Combat of the Thirty</a> in 1351. It ended with the Montfort victory at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-auray">Battle of Auray</a>, and the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerande">Guérande</a> in 1365 recognised John IV as duke.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-breton-succession.jpg" alt="War of the Breton Succession" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Auray.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
